{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git log -2 --format=fuller && rg -n 'jolt|transit|jvm|node|dart' test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj | head -45 && sed -n '1,55p' test/yin/vm/linker/head_board_test.cljc && sed -n '130,156p' src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc && sed -n '1410,1455p' src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"commit fd195c0cf0c7a62cd21915b8bcde3cb3e2231509\nAuthor:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nAuthorDate: Sun Nov 15 15:50:32 2026 -0500\nCommit:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nCommitDate: Sun Nov 15 15:50:32 2026 -0500\n\n    feat(dht): J7 slice 2 — DHT host composition on jolt and shell activation\n    \n    - Select `[dao.stream.udp :as datagram.host]` and `[dao.posix.random :as posix.random]` in `dao.space.dht` on `:jolt`.\n    - Implement `:jolt` arms in `default-bind` and `secure-random-bytes`.\n    - Service optional seam `:step!` in `dao.space.dht/step` before ticks and DHT processing.\n    - Standardize head board dial profile to CBOR with CBOR-first serving in `yin.shell.dht`.\n    - Remove the blanket jolt refusal in `yin.shell.dht/checked-spec`.\n    - Record engineer findings in `collab/jolt/1794775739000-engineer-j7-impl.findings.md`.\n    \n    Evidence:\n    - Solo DHT smoke: `echo '(+ 1 2)' | jolt -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-yin-repl --index-store dht:/tmp/j7-smoke` boots solo, evaluates to 3, publishes segment, and exits 0.\n    - All J7 namespaces load clean on Jolt (`dao.stream.udp`, `dao.stream.udp.common`, `dao.posix.random`, `dao.space.dht`, `yin.shell.dht`, `yin.repl`).\n    - JVM load and tests clean: `clojure -M -e \"(require 'yin.shell.dht 'yin.repl)\"` exits 0.\n\ncommit 16d4d3edb6e12c10b4cac13890fbda268b1a8e0a\nAuthor:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nAuthorDate: Sun Nov 15 15:49:34 2026 -0500\nCommit:     Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nCommitDate: Sun Nov 15 15:49:34 2026 -0500\n\n    feat(udp): J7 slice 1 — native UDP datagram host seam and facade factoring\n    \n    - Factor host-free value-channel functions into `dao.stream.udp.common`.\n    - Expose public facade `dao.stream.udp` delegating value-channel operations to `common` while retaining `UdpHandle` and `make-attacher`.\n    - Move qualified CSPRNG entropy implementation to `dao.posix.random` and delegate `yin.vm.linker.random` to it.\n    - Implement production native datagram `bind!` in `src/jolt/dao/stream/udp.jolt` with nonblocking SOCK_DGRAM, bounded owner `:step!`, immediate send syscall, failure pairs, IPv4/IPv6 literal parsing, and clean descriptor lifecycle.\n    \n    Evidence:\n    - JVM tests: `clojure -M:test -n dao.stream.udp-test -n dao.stream.udp-raw-test -n dao.stream.datagram-test` -> 37 tests, 185 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n    - Jolt J0b regression probe: `bb probe:jolt-udp` -> 37 assertions: 37 pass, 0 fail; 3 records.\n    - Jolt namespace load: `(require 'dao.stream.udp 'dao.stream.udp.common 'dao.posix.random)` -> loaded clean.\n14:   No port is reserved ahead of time.  The first node is an anchor in\n15:   this JVM (a `dao.jing.dht` core node over the JVM datagram seam,\n23:   `bb build:yin-repl-node`; a missing build fails this test.\n48:            [dao.stream.datagram.jvm :as datagram.jvm]\n163:  \"The first node: a `dao.jing.dht` core node on an ephemeral loopback\n172:         seam (datagram.jvm/bind! {:identity \"anchor\" :deposit traffic\n182:  #\"dht: node [0-9a-f]+ listening on 127\\.0\\.0\\.1:(\\d+)\")\n198:(defn- jvm-command\n209:(def ^:private node-script\n211:   built by `bb build:yin-repl-node`.\"\n241:   saved node state.\"\n242:  ([label args] (spawn! label (jvm-command) args))\n301:  ^:slow separate-jvm-processes-exchange-content-over-loopback\n433:                   node (dht/load-index\n438:                   node (loop\n439:                          [node node]\n441:                            [[node _] (dht/step\n442:                                        node\n445:                                                              node m)))\n447:                              node\n448:                              (do (Thread/sleep 10) (recur node)))))\n449:                   expected (try (dht/q node m remote-query)\n450:                                 (finally (dht/close! node)))]\n451:                  (is (= :loaded (:status (dht/load-status node m))))\n473:              (is (.exists (io/file node-script))\n474:                  (str \"the JVM-to-Node leg is required: \" node-script\n475:                       \" is absent; build it with `bb build:yin-repl-node`\"))\n476:              (when (.exists (io/file node-script))\n477:                (let [e (spawn! \"node-reader-e\" [\"node\" node-script]\n605:  \"Step the plain node with the wall clock until `(done? node)`: `[node\n606:   nil]`, or `[node cause]` when `ms` pass first.\"\n607:  [node ms cause done?]\n609:    (loop [node node]\n611:        (done? node) [node nil]\n612:        (> (System/currentTimeMillis) deadline) [node (str cause \" within \" ms\n614:        :else (let [[node _] (dht/step node (System/currentTimeMillis))]\n616:                (recur node))))))\n621:  (fn [node]\n622:    (contains? #{:loaded :failed} (:status (dht/load-status node address)))))\n691:     node (dht/join {:local (hiding (mem/create-content-mem) hidden)\n699:        [[node cause] (step-until (dht/load-index node m) exchange-ms\n702:         _ (is (= :loaded (:status (dht/load-status node m))))\n703:         names (ld/names node authority)\n710:          (is (= [m] (ld/snapshots node)))\n717:                                                node\n(ns yin.vm.linker.head-board-test\n  \"The head board over `dao.stream.remote-channel`, on loopback\n   (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md 5.1, section 6, slices H2 and\n   S3a-2).\n\n   The portable cases run over `dao.stream.loopback-net`, an in-process\n   stand-in for the host listener and connect seams.  One JVM case\n   crosses a real loopback socket through `yin.repl.host`.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.datom :as datom]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.dht.mesh :as mesh]\n            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n            [dao.space.dht :as dht]\n            [dao.space.index :as index]\n            [dao.space.transactor :as transactor]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.loopback-net :refer [blackhole! connect-on listen-on loopback-net pump! unbind-on unlisten!]]\n            [dao.stream.memory-log :as memory-log]\n            [dao.stream.remote :as remote]\n            [dao.stream.remote-channel :as rc]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n            [dao.stream.transit :as transit]\n            [dao.stream.ws-project :as ws-project]\n            [yin.vm.linker.dht :as ld]\n            [yin.vm.linker.head :as head]\n            [yin.vm.linker.head.board :as head.board]\n            [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]\n            #?@(:cljd []\n                :clj [[yin.repl.host :as host]]\n                :default [])))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Indexes at a chosen sequence (as in head-follow-test)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def p1 (sign/generate))\n\n\n(defn- principal\n  [key]\n  (sign/principal (:public key)))\n\n\n(defn- memory-log\n  []\n  (:dao.stream/handle\n    (memory-log/create! {:dao.stream/type memory-log/transport-type})))\n\n\n(defn- index!\n  [store history]\n  (let [intake (memory-log)\n        tx (transactor/create! {:local-stream (memory-log)\n   other reason is terminal.\"\n  #{::dht/too-few-peers ::dht/busy ::backlog-full ::publications-full})\n\n\n(defn default-bind\n  \"This build's datagram host seam (dao.stream.datagram.md section 3): the\n   JVM's, Node's `dgram` (required only when a socket binds, so a browser\n   build compiles), or Dart's.\"\n  []\n  #?(:jolt datagram.host/bind!\n     :cljd datagram.host/bind!\n     :cljs datagram.host/bind!\n     :clj datagram.host/bind!))\n\n\n(defn secure-random-bytes\n  \"`n` bytes from the host's cryptographically secure generator.\"\n  [n]\n  #?(:jolt (posix.random/rand-bytes n)\n     :cljd (let [r (math/Random.secure)]\n             (typed/Uint8List.fromList\n               (vec (repeatedly n #(.nextInt r 256)))))\n     :clj (let [bs (byte-array n)]\n            (.nextBytes (java.security.SecureRandom.) bs)\n            bs)\n     :cljs (.getRandomValues js/crypto (js/Uint8Array. n))))\n\n                                      [node (into events more)]))\n                                  [(assoc node :client state) []]\n                                  loading)]\n        ;; every load waiting on an address has read its miss cause: keep\n        ;; only the causes of addresses still being fetched\n        [(update node :misses select-keys (fetching node)) events]))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The public step and reads\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn step\n  \"Advance the node once at the owner's millisecond reading `now`:\n   append it as a tick; finish binding; admit repairs, then the puts and\n   announcements on the ledger ring; release replicate requests; step\n   the DHT; apply its facts; advance loads; and report publications.\n   Answers `[node' events]`.  A refused node (its socket could not bind)\n   is answered unchanged.\"\n  [node now]\n  (if (:refusal node)\n    [node []]\n    (let [_ (when-let [step-fn (get-in node [:seam :step!])]\n              (step-fn))\n          node (tick node now)\n          [node bound] (bind-step node)\n          node (admit-repairs node)\n          [node unknown] (admit-ledger node)\n          node (release node)\n          node (cond-> node (:dht node) (update :dht dht/step step-budget))\n          [node lost] (read-facts node)\n          [node loaded] (advance-loads node)\n          [node reported] (settle-publications node)]\n      [node (-> bound (into unknown) (into lost) (into loaded) (into\n                                                                 reported))])))\n\n\n(defn refusal\n  \"Why the node stopped (its socket could not bind), or nil.\"\n  [node]\n  (:refusal node))\n\n\n(defn backlog\n  \"What the node retains now: queue entries (`:fresh`, `:repair`),\n   requests outstanding (`:outstanding`, split `:outstanding-fresh` and\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
